**Keep monetary calculations in cents.**

`unitPrice` is already in cents. Dividing it by 100 introduces floating-point rounding error. A percentage discount can also produce fractional cents, despite the documented cent values.

Accumulate `unitPrice * quantity` as an integer. Apply the selected business rounding rule once when calculating the final cent total.

